        "original_id": "8e3a1077-fdb1-5df6-93bd-deef3cc88d65",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Organizations: ABBA\n- Songs: \"Money, Money, Money\", \"That's Me\", \"She's My Kind of Girl\"\n- Albums: \"Arrival\"\n- Musicals: \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n\nFacts:\n- Benny Andersson was born on 16 December 1946 and is a Swedish musician and composer.\n- Benny Andersson was a member of the Swedish music group ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Benny Andersson co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".\n- \"She's My Kind of Girl\" was written and performed by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus before they became famous as members of ABBA.\n- \"Money, Money, Money\" is a song recorded by ABBA and written by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus.\n- \"That's Me\" was released as a single in Japan the year after its original release with \"Money, Money, Money\" as the B-side to promote ABBA's album \"Arrival\".\n- \"That's Me\" reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.",
